# 2026-09-02 fourth follow-up, at Marco's explicit request: only one Stage-Server address to
# configure now, not two. There used to also be a separate VITE_COUCHDB_URL pointing at
# CouchDB's own port (6984) directly - removed, because browsers trust a self-signed cert per
# *origin* (scheme+host+port), not per-certificate, so every new tablet needed a *second*
# manual "trotzdem fortfahren" tap beyond the one for this address alone. core-backend now
# proxies CouchDB traffic through its own origin at a `/db` prefix (`index.ts`,
# `@fastify/http-proxy`, a pure passthrough - your own per-person CouchDB credentials still do
# all the real authenticating) and can also serve stage-pwa's own build output, so one accepted
# certificate covers the whole app, API, and database sync.
#
# No VITE_COUCHDB_USER/PASSWORD anymore (see #12): the PWA never holds admin CouchDB
# credentials. Per-person-accounts follow-up: there's no fixed, derivable CouchDB username
# per workspace either - every roster member has their own account, created via
# core-backend's POST /workspaces (founding) or POST /workspaces/:id/members (added later).
# Each device learns its own username/password once, either from that route's response
# directly (founding/adding a member on this device) or via the band's own access code
# (InviteBandView.tsx/JoinBandView.tsx) - never typed in by hand except through the
# "Passwort direkt eingeben" fallback.
#
# For tablets on the stage LAN, use the server's LAN address here instead of localhost (a
# tablet asking for localhost would ask itself). https:// once `scripts/generate-dev-certs.sh`
# has been run (see #34): getUserMedia()/WebMIDI need a secure context. Falls back to http://
# automatically on both the Vite and Fastify side if the certs haven't been generated. The
# server also needs the matching FRONTEND_ORIGIN env var set for CORS (only relevant while
# using Vite's own dev server - once core-backend serves stage-pwa's build directly, everything
# is same-origin and CORS no longer applies to app traffic at all). Just the build-time default
# now (Tier-A local-only-founding follow-up) - a device can point at a different Stage-Server at
# runtime via Einstellungen without a rebuild (stageServer.ts's getStageServerUrl()).
#
# stageboard.local (2026-09-02, at Marco's explicit request) - a friendly mDNS name instead of
# a raw IP, resolves for any device on the LAN once published via `/etc/avahi/hosts` on
# whichever machine runs the Stage-Server (docs/03 section 0a; a real domain would need
# internet/DNS infrastructure this project deliberately doesn't depend on - docs/02's
# "Zero-Friction Stage Requirement"). No port either: with `setcap cap_net_bind_service` granted
# to node (docs/03), core-backend can bind 443 directly - the browser default for https://,
# so it doesn't need to be written out. Both are one-time, per-machine setup steps, same as the
# certs themselves.
VITE_STAGE_SERVER_URL=https://stageboard.local
